Hunt for hardcoded or leaked secrets: API keys, tokens, passwords, private keys, connection strings, and credentials committed in source, config, or templates. The sink is any literal credential assigned to a variable, embedded in a URL/connection string, or returned/logged. Also flag endpoints or debug routes that echo secrets or config back to the caller. A secret does not have to look high-entropy — named constants like `admin_api_key = "..."` count.
